                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "How do I even review this product. It's not a game. This is surely what Valve were talking about when they mentioned \"Fake games\"\nThis was clearly a case of \"EA is in the dog house! So let's get a silly Loot box clicker game out ASAP, capitalise on the drama and make some moolar\" \n\nBox Looter 2018 is not a Loot box simulator. In this game every single loot box you open contains money of a higher value than the loot box itself. That's all they contain, in game currency which is displayed as USD. \nA proper Loot Box Sim would be more like a gambling simulator, surely. I was hoping there would be some form of planning ahead with my money, some risk, interesting loot inside of the boxes, but there isn't. \n\nIt's your average Steam bait clicker, except this time, you're clicking on loot boxes. Also the production value is non existent, the frame rate often dropped below 15fps when I was spam clicking boxes. \n\nSome of the Loot box names made me chuckle, so there's that. \nI opened a 'Raunchy Spinning Explosive Loot box.\n\nI bought and reviewed this piece of spunk filled gutter waste so that you don't have to. You can thank me later.\n[h1]0/5[/h1]\n\nPlease check out and follow my Steam Curator where I shine a light on the very best indie games and occasionally poke fun at some of the worst.\nhttp://store.steampowered.com/curator/31321063/",
